  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Science Applications International obligated $91.5M in federal contracts in FY2027 to date, across 69 awards with an average award size of $1.3M. Obligations fell 97.7% year over year compared with prior fiscal years. FY22 obligations were $3.9B. FY23 obligations were $4.4B. FY24 obligations were $4.5B. FY25 obligations were $4.5B. FY26 obligations were $4.1B. Top buying agencies so far in FY2027 include the Department of Justice at $33.1M and the Government Accountability Office at $19.8M, with the General Services Administration at $17.6M and the Department of Transportation at $14.5M. Top markets by NAICS for FY2027 include Other Computer Related Services at $33.1M, Engineering Services at $29.2M, and Computer Systems Design Services at $29.1M. The figures for FY2027 are partial, fiscal year to date, and some tables in the report use total contract values rather than obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the largest federal buyers of Science Applications International so far in FY2027?",
        "body": "The Department of Justice obligated $33.1M, the largest buyer in FY2027 to date. The Government Accountability Office obligated $19.8M and the General Services Administration obligated $17.6M. The Department of Transportation obligated $14.5M and the Department of Commerce obligated $7.8M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which markets and services account for Science Applications International's FY2027 obligations?",
        "body": "Other Computer Related Services is the largest market at $33.1M and Engineering Services follows at $29.2M. Computer Systems Design Services accounts for $29.1M and Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services accounts for $247K. Computer Facilities Management Services accounts for $25K."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Science Applications International make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Science Applications International has $91.5M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. Science Applications International received those obligations across 69 awards with an average award size of $1.3M, and obligations are down 97.7% year over year compared with prior fiscal years."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Science Applications International?",
      "a": "Science Applications International's largest buyers in FY2027 to date are the Department of Justice at $33.1M, the Government Accountability Office at $19.8M, and the General Services Administration at $17.6M. Science Applications International also has obligations from the Department of Transportation at $14.5M and the Department of Commerce at $7.8M."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Science Applications International sell to the government?",
      "a": "Science Applications International primarily sold Other Computer Related Services and Engineering Services in FY2027, with obligations of $33.1M and $29.2M respectively. Science Applications International also recorded $29.1M in Computer Systems Design Services and smaller amounts in consulting and facilities management markets."
    },
